    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f5722b36_3b14ef56",
        "filename": "util/flash_fp_mcu",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 301,
      "author": {
        "id": 1113904
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-19T20:12:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Interesting, so this is a delay between releasing of reset and the stm32mon doing stuff?\n\nOur board has a 10k pullup on this line, so I guess it\u0027s marginal/not fast enough?\n\nI would feel a lot better with this number if we had scope shots of this event (reset releasing vs cs asserting), together with perhaps a datasheet of the stm32 bootloader guide saying what the earliest time it\u0027s ready to accept commands is.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 301,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 301,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "2adb69157df6ca3d3a393751858709a66e842a17",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b0f277b6_07f81764",
        "filename": "util/flash_fp_mcu",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 301,
      "author": {
        "id": 1413538
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-20T22:05:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I couldn\u0027t get the scope shots for this event. I guess, we need to consider rise time with the pull up. Having 10K pull resistor and 0.1 uF capacitor, the rise time comes around to be 0.8473 ms. Issue fixes with delay of 1 ms. Surprisingly, even adding \u0027sleep 0\u0027 works and I guess system call overhead may provide enough delay by itself.",
      "parentUuid": "f5722b36_3b14ef56",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 301,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 301,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "2adb69157df6ca3d3a393751858709a66e842a17",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f979426b_910ef6b7",
        "filename": "util/flash_fp_mcu",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 301,
      "author": {
        "id": 1113904
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-20T22:51:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That would explain a lot, I missed that we had a capacitor.\n\nMatch checks out, we should use at least 1ms for that reset to deasserted. But that\u0027s not enough:\n\nLooking further: https://www.st.com/resource/en/application_note/cd00167594-stm32-microcontroller-system-memory-boot-mode-stmicroelectronics.pdf. Apparently we need at least a 16.63 ms + 1us delay between reset deasserting and bootloader being able to recieve stuff on SPI.\n\nSounds like we would want 20ms instead and it\u0027s a miracle it worked until now with nothing. It\u0027s probably just userspace/syscall delays the helped us so far.\n\nThis kind of discussion would be perfect to be captured in the commit message and/or code comment.",
      "parentUuid": "b0f277b6_07f81764",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 301,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 301,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "2adb69157df6ca3d3a393751858709a66e842a17",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2b87318a_7708d064",
        "filename": "util/flash_fp_mcu",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 301,
      "author": {
        "id": 1113904
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-20T23:01:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Addition: in my pdf you want to look at \"68 Bootloader timings\", the 16.63 ms value is 68.1, \"Table 146. Bootloader startup timings (ms) for STM32 devices\", row \"STM32F74xxx/75xxx\".\n\nThough checking again, I should have looked at \"STM32H74xxx/75xxx\" which is even worse! 53ms!\n\n1us is for the SPI interface stuf on 68.5.",
      "parentUuid": "f979426b_910ef6b7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 301,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 301,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "2adb69157df6ca3d3a393751858709a66e842a17",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
